You and your Organization are solely responsible for:
- the accuracy and completeness of everything entered into, uploaded to or connected with the Services;
- reviewing every report, calculation, check, payment, journal entry, payroll figure and AI-generated answer before relying on it or acting on it;
- complying with every law that applies to your business, including federal, state and local wage-and-hour, employment, tax, record-keeping, privacy, consumer-protection, banking and securities laws;
- obtaining any notices, consents and authorizations needed to put personal information about employees, guests, investors, vendors or others into the Services; and
- keeping your own copies of records that the law requires you to keep.

We do not sell personal information and we do not share it for cross-context behavioral advertising. We disclose it only:
- to service providers who host, store, email, secure or support the Services under contracts that limit their use of the data (our current list is in the Data Processing Addendum);
- to third-party services a customer chooses to connect, such as accounting software or bank-data providers;
- within a customer's organization, according to the permissions it sets;
- to comply with law, legal process or lawful government requests, or to protect the rights, safety and property of Akea, our customers or others; and
- in connection with a merger, acquisition, financing or sale of assets, subject to this policy.

- use the Services for anything unlawful, fraudulent, deceptive or harmful, including wage theft, falsifying time or financial records, check fraud, money laundering, or misleading investors or lenders;
- edit records to hide what happened instead of correcting them with a reason, or try to bypass the audit trails, approval steps or record-retention protections in the Services;
- access accounts, hotels or data you are not authorized to see, share your sign-in, or probe, scan or test the vulnerability of the Services without our written permission;
- upload malware, or interfere with or overload the Services;
- copy, frame, scrape or harvest the Services or their data by automated means, except through features we provide;
- reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the Services, or use them to build a competing product, except to the extent the law expressly allows this despite this restriction;
- resell, sublicense or provide the Services to third parties except as your subscription allows;
- upload full Social Security numbers, full bank or card numbers, health information, or other sensitive information the Services are not designed to hold;
- upload content you do not have the right to use, or that infringes someone else's intellectual property or privacy;
- share third-party licensed data, such as STR reports, outside the people your license allows;
- use the AI assistant to produce content that is unlawful or to make decisions about employment, credit, housing or other significant matters about a person without human review; or
- use the Services in violation of U.S. export-control or sanctions laws.
